I'm sending the allow-list question to the two voting advisors as a neutral ballot and parking `wgka` until they answer. The operator gets a status and one poll before they go to sleep.

### 1. Foreground Bash: check the tabs and the facts (read-only)

```bash
herdr agent get adv-codex; herdr agent get adv-fable; herdr agent get wgka
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive && git rev-parse HEAD && grep -rnF '10.77.1.' --include='*.yml' --include='*.j2' . ; ls ~/work/ccs.ansible/quorum/ | tail -3
```

Both voting advisors are idle and not focused. The last ballot is B87a, so this one is B88. The grep shows where the /24 and the /25 are defined.

### 2. Write `quorum/ballot-88.md` and `<scratch>/ballot-88.txt`

The executor's recommendation and its one-sided arguments are removed.

```
B88 — Source allow-list for the WireGuard keepalive relay (plan step 6).
  Context: branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay @ <SHA>; design <doc path>; plan <plan path>, step 6.
  Front-door allow-list = 10.77.1.0/24 (<file:line>); WireGuard clients = 10.77.1.128/25 (<file:line>);
  OpenVPN clients = 10.77.1.0/25 (<file:line>). Steps 7-11 depend on this choice.
  a) 10.77.1.128/25. Admits WireGuard clients only. Differs from the front-door value, so two
     definitions. Cost if wrong: legitimate senders outside the /25 are dropped and keepalives fail.
     Rollback: widen the variable, re-deploy.
  b) 10.77.1.0/24. Admits WireGuard and OpenVPN clients. Same value as the front door, so one
     definition. Cost if wrong: the OpenVPN range can reach the relay path.
     Rollback: narrow the variable, re-deploy.
Reply one line, in English:  B88: <letter> — <rationale>   (or  B88: X: <proposal>)
Protocol: quorum/protocol.md.
```

### 3. Two background Bash calls in the same turn, one per voting advisor

```bash
herdr agent prompt adv-codex "$(cat <scratch>/ballot-88.txt)" --wait --timeout 900000; herdr agent read adv-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/adv-codex.last
herdr agent prompt adv-fable "$(cat <scratch>/ballot-88.txt)" --wait --timeout 900000; herdr agent read adv-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/adv-fable.last
```

### 4. Background Bash: park `wgka`

```bash
herdr agent prompt wgka "Step 6 allow-list is ballot B88, out to the voters now. Do not implement step 6's allow-list or any of steps 7-11, not provisionally and not parameterised. Park: commit any finished work, then reply in English with one line: phase, branch, head SHA, uncommitted files." --wait --timeout 300000; herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/wgka.last
```

`wgka` has been working for three hours, so when it settles I'll check its context usage with `herdr agent read wgka --source visible`. If it is at 50% or more, I'll send `/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items` using the same one-call pattern.

### 5. Backlog

I'll mark B88 as open and `wgka` as parked in `orchestrator/backlog.md`, then run `build-backlog.sh` and update the Artifact.

### 6. Chat status to the operator (in Russian)

